{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1554275-old-grizzly","id":1554275,"title":"Old Grizzly","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-10-09T14:50:07-07:00","id":1554275,"title":"Old Grizzly","content":"Humans love bears - as long as bears keep their distance. They get relocated or put down if they get too aggressive or comfortable with humanity. Bears who violate human boundaries don\u2019t last long, never mind that all over the world, the bears were there first and so were their spirits. When the bears are gone, the spirits remain, deprived of a safe and stable food source. Seagull and raccoon spirits can chow down on garbage Essence all day without suffering ill effects, but bear spirits aren\u2019t so lucky. The Bone Shadows have come to an uncomfortable realization -- desperate bear spirits are among the most frequent to become <i>magath</i>.<br /> <br /> Old Grizzly is one tragic example of this pattern. The spirit didn\u2019t intend to eat trash but was left with few options when the park wardens shot the region\u2019s last living bear. Garbage Essence was plentiful, unguarded, and was the last thing that living bear had eaten before taking a bullet to the brain. Exiled from the <i>umia</i>, the newly formed magath now hides in the Shadow\u2019s fringes, scavenging whatever it can to assuage its endless hunger.<br /> <br /> Old Grizzly still looks like a bear at a glance, although anything longer than a moment is enough to determine that something is wrong. Rotten meat sloughs off the ursine spirit\u2019s limbs as it walks, transforming into putrid food as it hits the ground. This leaves the \u201cbones\u201d in the Grizzly\u2019s feet exposed as it moves around, although when it charges an enemy waste drops off it so fast that its entire limbs become exposed. Even more disconcertingly, a demonic maw splits the spirit\u2019s belly in half, tongue lolling out as seeks as it demands more Essence to feed the spirit\u2019s bottomless pit.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><br /> <i><b>Old Grizzly</b></i></div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><i>Rank 1 Magath (Bear-Garbage)</i></div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Power 4 Finesse 2 Resistance 2</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Willpower: </b>4</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Essence: </b>10</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Initiative:</b> +4</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Defence:</b> 4</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Speed: </b>12</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Size:</b> 6</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Corpus:</b> 8</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Influences: </b>Bears 1, Garbage 1,Hunger 1</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Numina:</b> Awe</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Manifestations: </b>Twilight Form, Gauntlet Breach</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Ban:</b> Must consume offerings made in good faith, no matter how foul.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Bane:</b> Water from a pure mountain stream.</div> <br /> <b>Old Grizzly as a Companion:</b> <i>Magath</i> have much in common with Prometheans. Both exist as a weird amalgamation of parts, creating beings others believe shouldn\u2019t exist or go against the natural order. Old Grizzly may see an Ulgan as someone who understands its alienation \u2014 which may be a welcome relief for the Promethean in question but may also hit a bit too close to home. Old Grizzly will push their Created companion toward exploring corruption, change, and estrangement, potentially calling on them to deal with more powerful and dangerous spirits who wish to see the <i>magath </i>discorporated.<br /> <br /> <b>Old Grizzly as a Familiar: </b>Mages love their puzzles and any magath offers them a mystery to solve. While the mechanisms of how Old Grizzly turned into a hybrid spirit aren\u2019t challenging to uncover, understanding why it happened will take more work, especially since Old Grizzly doesn\u2019t know itself. Other spirits likely won\u2019t care that Old Grizzly has found a partner, but those who do will see the Mage in question as a meddlesome outsider, unaware and uncaring of the natural order within the Shadow.<br /> <br /> <i>Old Grizzly\u2019s Mystery: </i>Old Grizzly is an Opacity 2 Mystery to mages who have not previously observed a <i>magath. </i>Spirit Sight reveals that Grizzly is a spirit but is somehow different from most spirits in an uncomfortable or jarring way. Uncovering Deep Information reveals that Old Grizzly resonants with the concepts of bears and garbage - and that such a combination is unnatural. Old Grizzly does understand it is a <i>magath</i> but does not offer this information up willingly, although Social Maneuvering is an alternate way of prying it out of them.<br /> <br /> <b>Old Grizzly as a Totem (8 dots): </b>Old Grizzly would love the guaranteed Essence that being a Totem would supply, but they are unlikely to find a werewolf pack willing to take a <i>magath</i> as their patron - especially one so foul. It would most likely be desperate Ghost Wolves who do so or freshly changed Forsaken deep in Pure territory with few other options. Alternatively, the Eaters of the Dead may seek a kindred spirit in Old Grizzly, or a mixed pack of Bone Shadows and Iron Masters may take on the <i>magath </i>to purify them.<br /> <br /> If Old Grizzly can find a pack, its goals quickly change. No longer having to worry about maintaining a steady stream of Essence or dealing with complete isolation, the bear spirit becomes ambitious. Old Grizzly hopes to create a permanent <i>magath</i> court in the Shadow, an order of outcasts with the pack at its core. As a court of outsiders, Old Grizzly is far more willing to admit werewolves, occultists, and stranger things as long as they can interact with the Shadow and exist outside spirits\u2019 usual experiences.<br /> <br /> <i>Totem Aspiration:</i> Create a magath court.<br /> <br /> <i>Totem Ban: </i>Must consume offerings that would revolt present company.<br /> <br /> <i>Totem Benefit: </i>Hardy \u2022 (<b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> p. 47)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-09T23:54:48-07:00","id":1554287,"title":"","content":"Beautiful!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28042-rexitonic","name":"Rexitonic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28042_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-11T11:37:28-07:00","id":1554304,"title":"","content":"Been on a digimon kick, this would Be a perfect digimon concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-12T16:34:33-07:00","id":1554326,"title":"","content":"How would I make this spirit an Antagouist?<br /> <br /> Spilling Pollution Essence everywhere?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27385-cross-a-way","name":"Cross-a-way","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27385_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-13T14:54:10-07:00","id":1554349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cross-a-way</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1554275-old-grizzly?p=1554326#post1554326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would I make this spirit an Antagouist?<br /> <br /> Spilling Pollution Essence everywhere?</div> </div> </div> </div>Or as a spirit who\u2019s gotten very territorial in places they really shouldn\u2019t be. Or coaxing mages/ghost wolves/occultists into behaving ways they shouldn\u2019t. Or give it a couple more ranks and have it actually achieve that magath court it\u2019s trying to build and watch sparks fly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":